many has included individuals who arrived from Ukraine since 24 February 2022 but who were still waiting a decision regarding their Temporary Protection application as well as those who had not yet formally applied for temporary protection or refugee status. The reason to include them was linked to the high number of arrivals of persons fleeing Ukraine into Germany, and the resulting prolonged waiting periods to process applications. Given that the number of applications has decreased over time as well as changes in the national legal framework, UNHCR considers that it is no longer reasonable to continue including these individuals in the figures of total refugees present in the country.","fn_314f1b25":"The figure does not represent the entire number of persons registered as stateless in the German Central Aliens Register. The number of stateless persons holding a humanitarian residence title (not all of whom are persons of concern to UNHCR) and the number of stateless asylum-seekers have been deducted from it.","fn_4e050d99":"The data do not include 736 Syrians who arrived under admission programmes established by the German Laender.","fn_7798d15f":"This figure is based on the number of stateless persons registered in the German Central Aliens Register as being “stateless”. The number of stateless persons counted as asylum seekers as well as the number of stateless counted under “refugee population” have been deducted. Persons registered under the category “undefined nationality” are not included in the statistics.","fn_9e13df70":"The figure does not represent the entire number of persons registered as stateless in the German Central Aliens Register. The number of stateless persons holding a humanitarian residence title (not all of whom are persons of concern to UNHCR) and the number of stateless asylum-seekers have been deducted from it.","fn_a47c49c0":"The Indo-Chinese population in China is no longer considered as refugees under UNHCR's mandate and has been removed from UNHCR's statistical reporting since June 2022, because they have full access to public services and enjoy the same rights as nationals.","fn_e1ccf697":"The figure does not represent the entire number of persons registered as stateless in the German Central Aliens Register. The number of stateless persons holding a humanitarian residence title (not all of whom are persons of concern to UNHCR) and the number of stateless asylum-seekers have been deducted from it."},"raw_files":{"demographics/2025.zip":{"label":"UNHCR API download (demographics/2025.zip)","header":["Year","Country of origin","Country of origin (ISO)","Country of asylum","Country of asylum (ISO)","Population Type","Female 0 - 4","Female 5 - 11","Female 12 - 17","Female 18 - 59","Female 60","Female other","Female total","Male 0 - 4","Male 5 - 11","Male 12 - 17","Male 18 - 59","Male 60","Male other","Male total","Total"]},"persons_of_concern.csv":{"label":"UNHCR Refugee Data Finder download (persons_of_concern.csv)","header":["Year","Country of Asylum","Country of Origin","Country of Asylum ISO","Country of Origin ISO","Refugees","Asylum-seekers","IDPs","Other people in need of international protection","Stateless persons","Host community","Others of concern"]}},"raw_rows":{"demographics/2025.zip#L3888":{"file_key":"demographics/2025.zip","line":3888,"row":["2025","Viet Nam","VNM","Germany","DEU","REF","31","17","24","1120","286","0","1478","30","20","21","1148","526","0","1745","3584"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L104851":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":104851,"row":["2020","Germany","Viet Nam","DEU","VNM","1138","248","0","0","0","0","0"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L110369":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":110369,"row":["2021","Germany","Viet Nam","DEU","VNM","1096","276","0","0","0","0","0"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L116044":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":116044,"row":["2022","Germany","Viet Nam","DEU","VNM","2858","283","0","0","0","0","0"]},"persons_of_concern.